From d5b111fd2140ea1bf07147d2c6ee8bce7449b092 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:32:02 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Calls to another of the person's computers take a direct link
 when one is up

Every call between devices crossed the edge's device-room relay, even
for a laptop and a PC on one network: a message's files to a chat on the
other computer too, and a relay link that drops every minute or two
could not carry them. Terminals already take a direct WebRTC link
(zeron_preview) when the two devices can reach each other.

direct_rpc.rs serves the same RPC over that link: one `rpc` stream of
newline-delimited JSON frames per connection.

- Host: served beside the relay host, with the relay's service and the
  relay's guard (zeron_rpc::device_room::peer_service, now public):
  local-only calls refused, the rest answered as an unverified peer's, as
  an unstamped relay dial's are. Cloud machines may not open one and
  don't serve one, as for terminals. Advertised as direct-rpc-v1.
- Client: a queued attachment's chunks, its UploadStatus and commit, and
  the command relay take the direct link when the host advertises it and
  the two are paired. Not paired yet: the relay carries the call and
  pairing starts, so a retry finds the link up; with the resumed
  transfers, a file moves from one road to the other without starting
  over.
- Nothing waits long on the direct road. A link that closed reads closed
  (RpcClient::is_closed: a clean close sets no close_reason), so a call
  is never handed to a dead one. Open links are pinged every 15 s and
  dropped when the far end stops answering, and closed after 5 minutes
  unused, as the relay's are. A stream that fails to open sends calls by
  the relay for 5 s, doubling to 60 s on failures in a row. Pairing is
  asked for at most every 30 s per device, doubling to 5 minutes while it
  never comes up. A stream opens on a task of its own, one per device at
  a time, so a call that stops waiting doesn't cut a pairing off half-way.
- The log says when calls to a device switch between the direct road and
  the relay.

Tests: direct_rpc's calls_cross_a_byte_stream_and_are_served_as_a_peers,
the_relays_refusals_hold_on_a_direct_link_too,
only_the_owners_own_computers_may_open_one,
the_host_end_holds_its_service_weakly,
a_client_whose_link_dropped_reads_closed and
waits_double_from_the_first_to_the_cap.
